WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:05.170
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
for my bonus video I wanted to go a little

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.740
deeper into the faith of the seven.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:11.950
So this will be about the Faith Militant.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:15.169
Mostly a history video but after I’ll explain
how I think the show might introduce them

00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:16.400
if they decide to use them.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.500
Not all the major organizations and mercenary
groups have been featured from the books.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:25.410
But Jonathan Pryce was cast as the High Sparrow,
the leader of the Church in King’s Landing.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:31.430
So presumably we’ll get a look at the inner
workings of the church in and around baelor’s

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.430
sept.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.710
If you’re just finding me for the first
time I’m doing weekly bonus videos till

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:35.710
season 5 gets here.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.170
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.051
I’m even doing a weekly book giveaway I’ll
explain at the end of the video.

00:00:41.051 --> 00:00:44.720
The Faith Militant are the militarized arm
of the Faith of the Seven, they’re made

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.590
up from two different subgroups inside the
church called the Warrior’s Sons and the

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.719
Poor Fellows.

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:52.920
You can imagine how they decide who gets to
be what.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.109
The Warrior’s Sons are made up of Knights
and other high born people that have sworn

00:00:56.109 --> 00:00:57.620
off their lands and titles.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.399
The swear their allegiance to the High Sparrow.

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:02.449
They get special armor just like the King’s
Guard.

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:06.710
And like the King’s Guard the most defining
characteristic of it is the cloak.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.860
The Warrior’s Sons wear Rainbow colored
cloaks just like the King’s Guard wear White

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.659
Cloaks and the City Watch wear Gold Cloaks.

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:20.700
Their armor is silver and their swords have
a star shaped crystals in the pommels.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.460
Stars as imagery of the seven pointed star
of the faith.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:28.100
They have a reputation for fanaticism like
you might see in the unsullied, with the big

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.470
difference that they all are uncut.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.570
Something about religious armies attracting
fanatics.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:34.310
That can’t be good.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.590
The Poor Fellows are made up of the peasantry.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.440
But they allow women in their ranks.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:45.329
They serve as lightly armored footmen and
instead of the really nice armor and weapons

00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:46.840
that the warriors son’s get.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.350
They just fight with whatever they can find.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:52.270
They don’t have an official weapon and they
don’t wear the rainbow cloaks.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:55.060
The military branches of the church have only
existed for certain periods in history but

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.159
they do predate Aegon’s Conquest.

00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:57.330
Even though the High Sparrow is like a Pope
of sorts, I don’t really think of the Warrior’s

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.330
Sons as the Swiss Guard.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:01:59.330
Those are the armed forces that protect the
real life Pope in Vatican City.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:00.409
The Faith Militant are a fully mobilized army
that at times have enforced the will of the

00:02:00.409 --> 00:02:01.409
acting High Sparrow.

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:03.960
There was even a conflict called the Faith
Militant Uprising after Aegon the Conqueror’s

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:04.960
Death.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.340
Because Aegon had openly married his two sisters
the Faith of The Seven viewed their children

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:12.820
as sinful abominations, so when Aegon’s
oldest son Aenys took the throne.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:16.510
The Faith launched an uprising to remove the
Targaryen’s from power.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:22.620
Aenys was described as a very weak king so
his half brother Maegor, the son of Aegon’s

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.750
other sister and acting hand of the king,
launched the crown’s campaign to eliminate

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:25.750
the faith militant.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.340
The uprising lasted all the way through Aenys
reign and Maegor who succeeded him instead

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.550
of Aenys son Jaehaerys the first.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.950
This was Maegor the First also known as Maegor
the cruel.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.280
He was the polar opposite of his brother Aenys.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.360
As a way to turn the populace against the
Faith Militant, he placed a price on each

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:39.360
of their heads.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:43.150
One Golden Dragon for the scalp of any Warrior’s
Son, remember they were the highborn knights

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:46.010
of the order and a Silver Stag for the scalp
of any Poor Fellow.

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:48.330
That act was what earned him the nickname
Maegor the Cruel.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.620
His reign was really interesting so we can
talk more about it when the new World of Ice

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:54.661
and Fire book comes out in October.

00:02:54.661 --> 00:02:58.610
It has complete family tree’s for the Targaryen’s
and the Starks.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:02.810
He died under very mysterious circumstances
while sitting on the Iron Throne.

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:07.090
He literally died while just sitting on the
throne.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.090
His reign only lasted for about 6 years.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:13.370
Both he and his brother Aenys died when they
were about Cersei and Jaime’s age.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:14.600
About mid 30s.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:19.730
After Maegor died, Aenys son took the throne
at the age of 14 and immediately offered Amnesty

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:24.430
to the Faith of the Seven if they agreed to
disband the two orders of the Faith Militant.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:30.980
The acting High Sparrow agreed and the conflict
was ended.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:36.100
Fun Fact, one of Maegor’s wives was named
Jeyne Westerling, in the books, Jeyne Westerling

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:39.070
is also the name of the woman Robb Stark marries.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.490
On the show they replaced that character with
Talisa Maegyr played by Oona Chaplin.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:46.290
So you can see how they change things on the
show but try to work in references to the

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.290
books.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:50.140
Westerling to Maegyr, which sounds a lot like
Maegor.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:53.930
Anyone who’s worried about George RR Martin
expanding A Song Of Ice and Fire to 8 books

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:58.620
instead of just 7, remember that it gives
him more room for flashbacks to things like

00:03:58.620 --> 00:03:59.620
this.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:05.480
Although he is also planning a novel series
told from the perspective of the Targaryen

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.620
Family after A Song of Ice and Fire is over.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:13.600
Thus far the show hasn’t really done flashbacks
like in the books, usually historical events

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.470
just get referenced in conversation.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:24.000
The High Sparrow controls the Faith Militant
and currently where we are on the show, they’ve

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.520
still been disbanded.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:31.650
The High Sparrow that Jonathan Pryce is playing
is the new one in Book 4.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.750
During Season 2 the previous High Septon was
ripped apart when the Mob attacked Joffrey

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:35.750
in the streets.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:36.840
They ripped his arm off on the show.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.650
After that happened Tyrion appointed the new
High Sparrow.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:43.310
That one was also eventually killed before
the one Jonathan Pryce is playing comes into

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.310
the story.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:46.190
We saw Tyrion’s High Septon perform his
wedding to Sansa and Joffrey and Margeary’s

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:47.190
wedding ceremony.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.980
In the timeline, he would have become High
Sparrow some time before the Battle of Blackwater.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:51.430
The shows already changed a lot, so it’s
unclear how they’re going to deal with the

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:55.140
transition from High Septon number 2 to High
Septon number 3.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.760
After Tyrion’s High Septon is killed mysteriously,
the faith itself chooses the next High Septon,

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:05.220
that’s the character Jonathan Pryce is playing.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:11.120
The reason he’s nicknamed the High Sparrow
is because he’s chosen from amongst a group

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:15.130
of the poorest members of the faith that enter
king’s landing pleading for protection during

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:16.620
the war of the five kings.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:20.950
They collectively take the name Sparrows,
so they’re referred to as The Sparrows,

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:23.470
thus the new High Septon is called High Sparrow.

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:25.320
There was a lot of shit going down in that
finale.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:29.150
So it’s possible season 5 could pick up
and Jonathan Pryce will already be the High

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:30.310
Septon.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:34.210
The show has a history of just brushing over
minor characters and the previous high septon

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:41.940
the one that did all the weddings, wasn’t
really featured that much.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:45.180
Even though the show is changing a lot of
things Jonathan Pryce’s character will probably

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:48.620
have a lot of the broad strokes of the High
Sparrow from Book 4.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:52.460
Because septon’s give up their name when
they’re appointed High Septon, no one knows

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:53.460
his true identity.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:56.930
I know there are a lot of rumors and theories
about the High Sparrow being a very unlikely

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:59.433
character in disguise but if you have read
the books and want to talk about specific

00:05:59.433 --> 00:06:01.550
things, just use spoiler tags in the comments.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:05.300
Season 5 on the show is really the beginning
of uncharted territory in terms of book story.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.890
So once we get to season 6 it will be a lot
easier for any of you that only watch the

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:10.780
